/*!
\page page_sttrackgeometry StTrackGeometry

\brief Abstract interface for track helix geometry at a reference point.

\section sttrackgeometry_overview Overview

\ref StTrackGeometry is the abstract base class for all helix-parameter representations
of reconstructed charged-particle tracks in STAR.  It defines a uniform accessor API —
charge, curvature, dip angle, momentum, origin — without committing to a specific
parameterisation.  The concrete implementation is \ref StHelixModel.

Every \c StTrack holds two \c StTrackGeometry* pointers: one at the innermost measured
point (inner helix) and one at the outermost point (outer helix).

\section sttrackgeometry_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackGeometry   (abstract)
           └── StHelixModel
\endcode

\section sttrackgeometry_interface Pure Virtual Interface

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| \c model() | Geometry model identifier (\c kHelixModel). |
| \c charge() | Electric charge (+1 or −1). |
| \c helicity() | Helix sense: h = −sign(qB). |
| \c curvature() | Signed curvature κ (cm⁻¹). |
| \c psi() | Azimuthal momentum angle ψ at the origin (rad). |
| \c dipAngle() | Dip angle λ = arctan(p_z/p_T) (rad). |
| \c origin() | Reference point on the helix (cm). |
| \c momentum() | Momentum vector at the origin (GeV/c). |
| \c helix() | Full \c StPhysicalHelixD parameterisation. |
| \c copy() | Virtual copy constructor. |

\section sttrackgeometry_bad Validity Check

\c bad() returns non-zero when the helix is geometrically invalid (origin outside STAR
acceptance, zero momentum).

\section sttrackgeometry_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StTrackGeometry* geo = track->geometry();
if (!geo || geo->bad()) return;

double pt  = geo->momentum().perp();   // p_T [GeV/c]
double eta = /* from dipAngle */;

StPhysicalHelixD helix = geo->helix();
double s = helix.pathLength(/* target */);
\endcode

\see StHelixModel
\see StTrack
*/
